<title>UK: EIB sets 300 million mark bond due December 2001.</title>
<headline>EIB sets 300 million mark bond due December 2001.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Credit Suisse First Boston and SBC Warburg on Wednesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    300 MLN DEM   COUPON     4.50	MATURITY    28.DEC.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.02    PAY DATE    20.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.87     SPREAD	+18 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    FRANKFURT PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMANY   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.15	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND BOBL 120</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
